From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:47:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ship OpenFst's licence in the wheel's dist-info

setup.py links a system OpenFst (fst, fstscript, fstfar, fstfarscript,
fstmpdtscript, fstpdtscript) built separately -- this repo carries no
OpenFst source of its own, and third_party/Dockerfile fetches, builds
and installs it before building the wheel. auditwheel then bundles
those shared libraries into pynini.libs/ inside the wheel, as verified
against the real pynini-2.1.7-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_27_x86_64.
manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl from PyPI (165 MB, ~440 MB of libfst*.so
under pynini.libs/).

setup.py declares no `license_files`, so setuptools' default
LICEN[CS]E*/AUTHORS* root glob is what ships pynini's own LICENSE and
AUTHORS; it never reaches OpenFst's COPYING (Apache-2.0), which only
exists in the OpenFst tarball fetched at build time and is not part of
this checkout. Reproduced against that same real wheel: dist-info/
licenses/ carries only AUTHORS and LICENSE.

Restoring OpenFst 1.8.4's COPYING text unchanged as LICENSE.openfst at
the project root is picked up by that same default glob with no
packaging change, landing it in dist-info/licenses/ alongside pynini's
own LICENSE and AUTHORS.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no fork of kylebgorman/pynini to push from]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.openfst | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.openfst

diff --git a/LICENSE.openfst b/LICENSE.openfst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..511ac14
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.openfst
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
+you may not use these files except in compliance with the License.
+You may obtain a copy of the License at
+
+    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
+
+Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
+distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
+WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
+See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
+limitations under the License.
+
+Copyright 2005-2024 Google LLC.
